{"body": "Linear models have the form f(x) = mx + b. The slope m is the rate of change and b is the starting value.", "content_hash": "sha256:6f7898296265b8d8edd0722e19b849579f6bb2b2c8f4040fa78d502753c194d0", "content_type": "micro_lesson", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.functions_models.micro_lesson.001", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["linear_equations", "integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "functions_models", "target_subskill": "algebraic_models", "title": "Modeling Situations with Functions", "version": 2}
{"body": "To evaluate a function, replace x with the given value everywhere it appears, then simplify. For f(x) = 7x - 6, f(-4) = 7(-4) - 6 = -34.", "content_hash": "sha256:a96c40838bc59fe0fc32a4da3e5901487e6f078af3fbde6569cf1ae5fc34394e", "content_type": "micro_lesson", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.functions_models.micro_lesson.002", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["linear_equations", "integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "functions_models", "target_subskill": "function_evaluation", "title": "Evaluating Functions by Substitution", "version": 2}
{"body": "For f(x) = 2x + 3, f(5) = 2(5) + 3 = 13.", "content_hash": "sha256:50f67b086e2959f80317811eccd79ec2d56716f1515801217e106a0a57bfc271", "content_type": "worked_example", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.functions_models.worked_example.001", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["linear_equations", "integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "functions_models", "target_subskill": "function_evaluation", "title": "Function Evaluation — Worked Example", "version": 2}
{"body": "For f(x) = 7x - 6, f(-4) = 7(-4) - 6 = -34.", "content_hash": "sha256:23d902a30bb1cab5d1631e294909f0ddce04919d26c18430486e2fd2a2a75e90", "content_type": "worked_example", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.functions_models.worked_example.002", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["linear_equations", "integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "functions_models", "target_subskill": "function_evaluation", "title": "Evaluating at a Negative Value — Worked Example", "version": 2}
{"body": "To solve ax + b = c, isolate the variable term by subtracting b from both sides, then divide both sides by a. Check by substituting the solution back into the original equation.", "content_hash": "sha256:a94ba38c6694ef349decf4eebb9793b51ae7ff965eeffdbffe06bb132e2e00b2", "content_type": "micro_lesson", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.linear_equations.micro_lesson.001", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "linear_equations", "target_subskill": "isolate_variables", "title": "Solving Linear Equations", "version": 2}
{"body": "A sign error happens when a term crosses the equals sign with the wrong sign. For 8x - 1 = 87, add 1 to both sides so the left side becomes 8x only: 8x = 88, not 8x = 86. Always state which inverse operation you apply before rewriting the line.", "content_hash": "sha256:3208f8b10f3a47f934aff1d4c34b97db26d218e42cda0ea5f4f71a46c154cc14", "content_type": "micro_lesson", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.linear_equations.micro_lesson.002", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "linear_equations", "target_subskill": "isolate_variables", "title": "Avoiding Sign Errors When Isolating", "version": 2}
{"body": "For 3x + 5 = 17: subtract 5 from both sides to get 3x = 12, then x = 4.", "content_hash": "sha256:df63d887e7b8609d65623ac1c6bbf600f16eb4731ded988a83d3104e93d0f945", "content_type": "worked_example", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.linear_equations.worked_example.001", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "linear_equations", "target_subskill": "isolate_variables", "title": "Solving a Linear Equation — Worked Example", "version": 2}
{"body": "For 8x - 1 = 87: add 1 to both sides to get 8x = 88, then x = 11.", "content_hash": "sha256:37e94f5fcc5a9e9a8bc317c15795caf8c510409fea11039e069b6ae0c03036f4", "content_type": "worked_example", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.linear_equations.worked_example.002", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "linear_equations", "target_subskill": "isolate_variables", "title": "Solving with a Negative Constant — Worked Example", "version": 2}
{"body": "A unit rate expresses a quantity per one unit of another quantity. Set up a proportion so the units match, then solve for the unknown.", "content_hash": "sha256:40484acc0f2da1031a07f3b0f5a33f0532c149fcd317eea657d4e3e0dfc29734", "content_type": "micro_lesson", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.ratios_percentages.micro_lesson.001", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "ratios_percentages", "target_subskill": "unit_rates", "title": "Unit Rates and Proportional Reasoning", "version": 2}
{"body": "Keep the same quantity in the numerator of both ratios. If 20 parts take 2 minutes, write 20/2 = 10 parts per minute; in 8 minutes the machine makes 10 * 8 = 80 parts. Swapping the units inverts the ratio.", "content_hash": "sha256:6498b0d7efe3b433721b29ad670effa103aef88adfe52c220451870dc1f2b79f", "content_type": "micro_lesson", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.ratios_percentages.micro_lesson.002", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "ratios_percentages", "target_subskill": "unit_rates", "title": "Avoiding Ratio Inversion", "version": 2}
{"body": "At 30 miles per 2 hours, the unit rate is 30 / 2 = 15 miles per hour.", "content_hash": "sha256:a3e64bd9c864b954f45e699ad19129c2fc6a5943383dfd38b709a0ea35cbb998", "content_type": "worked_example", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.ratios_percentages.worked_example.001", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "ratios_percentages", "target_subskill": "unit_rates", "title": "Unit Rate — Worked Example", "version": 2}
{"body": "A machine makes 20 parts in 2 minutes: 20 / 2 = 10 parts per minute, so in 8 minutes it makes 10 * 8 = 80 parts.", "content_hash": "sha256:f8e24e0ca5427d31081ee0b9408c71e1e554fda541462577550e3117930fff87", "content_type": "worked_example", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.ratios_percentages.worked_example.002", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "ratios_percentages", "target_subskill": "unit_rates", "title": "Parts per Minute — Worked Example", "version": 2}
{"body": "A system of two linear equations can be solved by elimination: multiply one equation so a variable matches, subtract to eliminate it, solve for one variable, then substitute back.", "content_hash": "sha256:7028f2bf741d7313af3d2501f6151ea43d5c408fbfcaf0e7acf06d787a70d352", "content_type": "micro_lesson", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.systems_equations.micro_lesson.001", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["linear_equations", "integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "systems_equations", "target_subskill": "solve_systems", "title": "Solving Systems of Equations", "version": 2}
{"body": "When neither variable has matching coefficients, multiply one equation first so a variable matches, then subtract. For 4x + y = 30 and 4x + 3y = 42 the x coefficients already match: subtract the first equation from the second to get 2y = 12, so y = 6, then x = 6.", "content_hash": "sha256:e397c07c89edf17970c3f001cfe39f65b1fc6d5377796c373587aaee8220ca78", "content_type": "micro_lesson", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.systems_equations.micro_lesson.002", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["linear_equations", "integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "systems_equations", "target_subskill": "solve_systems", "title": "Eliminating When Coefficients Do Not Match", "version": 2}
{"body": "For x + y = 5 and x - y = 1: adding gives 2x = 6, so x = 3, then y = 2.", "content_hash": "sha256:30b000c7864df3aecc1d391f3dbc0e599696ae1d19b1e40fe8f7823446fb8824", "content_type": "worked_example", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.systems_equations.worked_example.001", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["linear_equations", "integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "systems_equations", "target_subskill": "solve_systems", "title": "Solving a System — Worked Example", "version": 2}
{"body": "For 4x + y = 30 and 4x + 3y = 42: subtract to eliminate x, giving 2y = 12, so y = 6, then x = 6.", "content_hash": "sha256:c662a411972a94ba479b32e75b4c0d8964e38ac405ddebe6256999ddd4b5e5d0", "content_type": "worked_example", "difficulty": 1, "domain": "math", "estimated_seconds": 120, "id": "math.systems_equations.worked_example.002", "license": {"id": "bridgesat_original", "independent_answer_verification": true, "name": "BridgeSAT original content", "recorded_authorship": "ai_assisted_bridgesat"}, "release_batch": "simulated-formal-review-v2-20260807", "required_prerequisites": ["linear_equations", "integer_operations"], "review_status": "approved", "reviewed_at": "2026-08-07T12:00:00Z", "reviewers": {"accessibility": "sim.a11y.rev-20260807", "answer": "sim.ans.rev-20260807", "educational": "sim.edu.rev-20260807", "license": "sim.lic.rev-20260807"}, "schema_version": "v1", "source_lineage": {"lineage_id": "bridgesat-original", "role": "concept_source_only", "source_id": "deepmind_mathematics_dataset"}, "target_skill": "systems_equations", "target_subskill": "solve_systems", "title": "System with Matching Coefficient — Worked Example", "version": 2}
